<title>NORWAY: FORECAST--Statistics Norway sees '97 CPI 2.4 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST--Statistics Norway sees '97 CPI 2.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Norwegian central bureau of statistics gave the following quarterly forecasts for key economic indicators:</p>
<p>(Percentage changes, previous forecast for comparison)</p>
<p>						June	 February</p>
<p>					   1997  1998    1997 1998</p>
<p> GDP (includes oil, gas)	    3.1   4.2     3.1  3.0</p>
<p> GDP mainland			   2.8   3.2     2.7  2.7</p>
<p> Private consumption		  2.5   2.6     3.1  2.7</p>
<p> Public consumption		   3.1   1.9     2.6  1.7</p>
<p> Export				   3.3   6.2     5.0  4.0</p>
<p> -oil and gas			   4.8   8.9     5.6  4.8</p>
<p> -Traditional goods		   3.8   5.1     5.5  5.0</p>
<p> Import				   4.4   3.0     6.5  3.4</p>
<p> -Traditional goods		   2.9   3.1     4.5  3.1</p>
<p> Unemployment rate		    4.2   4.0     4.5  4.3</p>
<p> CPI					2.4   1.8     1.8  1.2</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
